.TH CHTTPCLI_DO_POOLED_STREAMING 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_do_pooled_streaming \- do an HTTP request on the shared Tier 2 engine and stream the response body, and block until it finishes
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval chttpcli_do_pooled_streaming(chttpcli cli,
                                               const chttp_request *req,
                                               chttpcli_write_fn write_fn,
                                               void *write_ctx,
                                               int *status_code_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This is a thin wrapper over chttpcli_do_async_streaming that takes
the same arguments as chttpcli_do_streaming. write_fn runs on one of
the engine's reactor threads and not on the caller's thread, so the two
rules of chttpcli_do_async_streaming apply: write_fn must not block,
and it must not call back into the engine. That thread is the only
difference from chttpcli_do_streaming, whose callback runs on the
caller's thread. Calling chttpcli_destroy on any client (cli or
another one) from inside write_fn is a fatal error, because write_fn
runs on an engine thread; see chttpcli_destroy(3).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cli             The client handle. It must not be CHTTPCLI_NULL.
req             The request to run. It must not be NULL.
write_fn        The callback that gets each chunk. It must not be
                NULL.
write_ctx       An opaque context pointer that the client passes to
                write_fn unchanged.
status_code_out Receives the HTTP status code when the call
                succeeds. It can be NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The same codes as chttpcli_do_pooled, except that this function
never returns ccol_msg_too_large, because
chttpcli_set_max_response_body_size has no effect on a streaming
request.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_do_streaming (3),
.BR chttpcli_do_async_streaming (3),
.BR chttpcli_do_pooled (3)
